TLS fixtures for the binary checks -- test material, never trust them.

  ca.crt      a throw-away CA ("mcp-hub smoke-test CA (never trust)"); its key was
              deleted after signing
  server.crt  127.0.0.1, ::1 and localhost, signed by ca.crt
  server.key  the key of server.crt (public on purpose: anyone can read it here)
  le-r11.crt  Let's Encrypt's real intermediate R11, issued by ISRG Root X1, valid
              2024-03-13 to 2027-03-12 (SHA-256 fingerprint 59:1E:9C:E6:C8:63:D3:A0:
              79:E9:FA:BE:14:78:C7:33:9A:26:B2:12:69:DD:E7:95:21:13:61:02:4A:E3:1A:44),
              from https://letsencrypt.org/certs/2024/r11.pem -- public, nothing secret

ca.crt and server.crt are EC P-256 / SHA-256 and valid from 2026-01-01 to 2126-01-01,
so no clock and no expiry breaks the checks. scripts/loaded-modules.pl and
scripts/smoke-binary.sh run a hub that listens on https with server.crt/server.key
and trust ca.crt through SSL_CERT_FILE; t/binary.t keeps the pair working.
scripts/smoke-binary.sh verifies le-r11.crt against the trust store the binary finds
on the host, at 2025-01-01: a real chain checked without network.

ca.crt, server.crt and server.key were made with OpenSSL 3.5:

  cat >ca.cnf <<'EOF'
  [req]
  distinguished_name = dn
  prompt = no
  x509_extensions = v3_ca
  [dn]
  CN = mcp-hub smoke-test CA (never trust)
  [v3_ca]
  basicConstraints = critical, CA:TRUE, pathlen:0
  keyUsage = critical, keyCertSign, cRLSign
  subjectKeyIdentifier = hash
  EOF
  cat >server.ext <<'EOF'
  basicConstraints = critical, CA:FALSE
  keyUsage = critical, digitalSignature
  extendedKeyUsage = serverAuth
  subjectAltName = IP:127.0.0.1, IP:::1, DNS:localhost
  subjectKeyIdentifier = hash
  authorityKeyIdentifier = keyid
  EOF
  openssl genpkey -algorithm EC -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:P-256 -out ca.key
  openssl req -new -x509 -config ca.cnf -key ca.key -sha256 \
    -not_before 20260101000000Z -not_after 21260101000000Z -out ca.crt
  openssl genpkey -algorithm EC -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:P-256 -out server.key
  openssl req -new -key server.key -subj '/CN=127.0.0.1' -out server.csr
  openssl x509 -req -in server.csr -CA ca.crt -CAkey ca.key -set_serial 0x4d43502d487562 \
    -sha256 -not_before 20260101000000Z -not_after 21260101000000Z \
    -extfile server.ext -out server.crt
  rm ca.key server.csr
